            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Relationship with the Schumanns</strong><br>\nA significant early influence on Brahms was the composer Robert Schumann and his wife, Clara, who was an accomplished pianist and composer herself. Brahms formed a deep and lasting friendship with Clara, particularly after Robert's mental health declined.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Career Highlights</strong><br>\nBrahms's reputation grew with the success of works such as his German Requiem, symphonies, and concertos. He became renowned for his ability to blend the structure of classical music with the emotion of the romantic era, creating works with both intellectual depth and rich feeling.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life</strong><br>\nDespite his successful career, Brahms's personal life was marked by solitude. He never married and held his private life with guarded intimacy. He was known to have been close to several women throughout his life but maintained an independent and sometimes solitary existence.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
